Check whether services are running

You already know systemctl.

Manually:

systemctl is-active ssh

Depending on your Ubuntu installation, the service may be:

systemctl is-active ssh

or:

systemctl is-active ssh.service

Python can execute this program

import subprocess


result = subprocess.run(
    ["systemctl", "is-active", "ssh"],
    capture_output=True,
    text=True
)

print(result.stdout)

If SSH is running, you'll see:

Output: active

